WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.818
Good morning John. It is morning, which it usually is not when I make... when I say that out loud.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.559
I'm going to take you through a day in the life of me. I just did all my morning baby stuff

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.359
and now I'm coming up to the office. I don't have anything on my calendar until around eleven, so until then arrives,

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.699
I'm working on a song, which I haven't done in a while.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.220
I was gonna try to do it as a Song Wednesday, but [strums chord] it's just not happenin'.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.180
All right, songwriting over. I did put it on my Tumblr; it still has some problems, but if you want to listen to it

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.249
it's there. Now it's time to choose which Pizzamas shirt I'm gonna put on. I chose this drippy pizza.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.239
Time to go make s—

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:40.049
I forgot my computer! Everyone at work will be shocked, shocked! when I am late for the first meeting of the day,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:46.079
which I am, at the DFTBA warehouse. We're having our staff meeting, there's a pretty snowy mountain out there.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.480
That's nice

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.780
Dftba.com figures out how to make cool stuff for online creators and also how to get that stuff to people who want it. Basically, in this

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:57.839
meeting we had a bunch of cool ideas for cool things to make and then we talked about how the things that we are currently

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.300
making are doing. Everyone is very excited about Pizzamas. This is Rachel, she designs the socks, too.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.300
Hello.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.720
You can tell by her shirt

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.220
My everything.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:06.880
[Several people laugh]

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.660
This is just a frickin' great 2017 license plate right there.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.340
[Singing:] Work!

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.140
Candy corn flavored M&amp;Ms?!

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:13.880
Eeeew...

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.000
That's not good. They're the—SO bad. Tastes like...

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.360
...you, like... "I have no strong opinions on M&amp;M's"?

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.620
This was a mistake! I gotta go to a staff meeting.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.300
I beat you.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:23.980
You did!

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.020
Upstairs at our main office

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.939
we have the events team, mostly VidCon,

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:32.609
but also PodCon; this staff meeting was gathering to talk about the new space the Anaheim Convention Center has,

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:38.140
some PodCon marketing ideas so we can sell more tickets, and the trip that two people took to see how BlizzCon uses the

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:44.480
Convention Center in Anaheim so we can steal ideas from BlizzCon. It was about now that I realized that I had no scheduled time for lunch;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.540
luckily, that meeting ended soon, so I went and got a burrito.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.720
I mean...

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:50.220
Yes!!

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.240
They just painted this on this building, and as they were doing it, I noticed...

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.200
Different spacing on the sides! Oh god, it's gonna be there forever.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.060
Glumpkins

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.820
[Singing:] Goin' down to the studi—oh my god, it's cold down here. I always forget. I need

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.080
wardrobe

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.580
my shirts

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.320
I really enjoy shooting SciShow and Crashcourse, even if it is...

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.800
pretty draining? The scripts are always

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.320
really good these days, our writing staff is

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:19.180
legitimately one of the best in popular science writing, in my opinion. We shot a bunch of scripts including one about animals we thought

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:25.000
were extinct but weren't, uh, for SciShow, and one about why gratitude is so good for people for SciShow Psych.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.800
Which is our new psychology channel.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.660
Now I'm going to How to Adult. [Weird voice:] How to Adult! How to Adult is one of our less well-known

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.380
channels. This video that we were making today was on how to create and send good

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:39.069
thank-you cards. That one, unsurprisingly, will come out around Thanksgiving. Alright I'm done shooting,

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:44.289
it's 3:26. So I have a half an hour before—big staff meeting!—during which I can...

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.500
maybe answer emails? I don't know; we'll find out.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.459
Writing good emails is a... is a learned skill. Some people are very good at it.

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:54.578
This is a good email somebody sent me. Bad... bad news email for me,

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.180
but it was done really well. Good job, person! Pocky! All the flavors!

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.820
There's still a chair, still a chair!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:07.059
And then we had our big all-staff meeting, which we only do once a month. Here, the VidCon, DFTBA, and Complexly staffs all get

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.079
together to keep each other up to date on the big picture of what's happening at each company.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.340
I feel like these staff meetings could be super boring,

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:19.560
but, actually, they're very entertaining, and I find them to be one of my favorite times of the day,

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:26.000
which is, I feel like not usually how staff meetings go. [Burp] And now I go home! I just finished my burrito.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.660
[Weird voice:] Gotta put a baby to bed!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.740
Baby is in bed, I had dinner, back up to my office to... (take a phone call, and) edit a video!!

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:33.840
So that's usually roughly

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.780
how my days go, lots of meetings, lots of shooting, uh, and some

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:41.620
creative process, eh, thrown and usually they don't end up with me editing a video at 10 o'clock at night,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:47.410
but it's Pizzamas, and I'm not complaining. John I honestly can't wait to see what you come up with tomorrow.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.939
It's so fun to have, like, some creative pressure. I mean it's hard, but it's fun.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.149
I love Pizzamas. And I'll see what you got for me tomorrow.

